== restclient
# name: login
POST https://{{host}}/login
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
[Form]
user: {{username}}
pass: s3cret value

# name: profile
GET https://{{host}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login_response_body___token}}
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

# name: Upload avatar
POST https://{{host}}/avatar
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=boundary123
[Multipart]
title: hello
file: file,./pic.png; image/png

# name: Raw file body
POST https://{{host}}/blob
Content-Type: application/octet-stream
[Options]
output: ./out/blob-response.json
file,./blob.bin;
== sonde.yaml
version: 1
environments:
  default:
    variables:
      apiKey: '{{$dotenv API_KEY}}'
      host: example.test
      username: ""
defaults:
  env: default
warning unsupported: file variable "apiKey" resolves to "{{$dotenv API_KEY}}", which sonde.yaml cannot expand further; set it directly or via --variable
warning unsupported: {{login.response.body.$.token}} references another request's request or response; use a Sonde capture instead
warning unsupported-body: "<@ ./blob.bin" has the source tool substitute its own variables inside the file before sending; Sonde's file body sends it as is, so those "{{...}}" are not substituted
warning unsupported-option: @prompt username: no interactive prompt at import time; set the username variable yourself
warning unsupported-option: Raw file body: ">> ./out/blob-response.json" never overwrites an existing file in JetBrains (it adds a numeric suffix instead); Sonde's "output:" always overwrites
